  "_README": [
    "Recorded KONE API responses, keyed by request path.",
    "",
    "Field names are copied verbatim from KONE's published TypeScript",
    "interfaces in github.com/konecorp/kone-api-examples (src/common/types.ts,",
    "commit e597b46, Nov 2025) - GetServiceOrder, ListServiceOrder, Status,",
    "Availability and Movement. The VALUES are invented for this prototype;",
    "the KEYS are KONE's.",
    "",
    "That split is the whole point: the adapters' mapping logic is the part",
    "that breaks if the published schema was misread, and running it against",
    "these keys exercises exactly that. It cannot substitute for one live",
    "call - it will not catch a documented field the service omits, a",
    "pagination envelope the examples do not show, or an insufficient scope.",
    "",
    "SO-4412884 is a PLANNED replacement with no fault - the censored case. A sheave renewed under a modernization programme is a routine KONE service order, and it is precisely where the API records that a component came out and nothing about where it went. Omitting it made the label harvester look better covered than it is."
